When you use
`routeLoader$` the default behavior is to wait for it to complete before rendering our component(s).
However, there is a way to render the DOM up to the point where
`routeLoader$` is used and wait for it to complete.
By returning an asynchronous function from our
`routeLoader$` we can stream/defer the rendering to provide immediate visual feedback.
